sequenceDiagram
%% DOC-03 — Sequence: import, validate, match and recommend (UC-01..03, P1..P5)
%% Every system step writes its audit event in the same transaction (CR-08).
    autonumber
    actor S as Staff Accountant
    participant UI as Web UI
    participant RUN as Run service
    participant VAL as Validation and normalization
    participant RUL as Rules engine
    participant SCO as Scoring engine
    participant RSK as Risk and routing
    participant DB as Database D1–D7
    participant AUD as Audit log D9

    S->>UI: Upload bank, GL and carry-in CSV (UC-01)
    UI->>RUN: Start run (account 7310, Aug 2026)
    RUN->>DB: Store files, hash, control totals (D1)
    RUN->>AUD: IMPORT events
    RUN->>VAL: Validate files
    VAL->>DB: Record tests and results (D3)
    VAL->>AUD: VALIDATION events
    alt File-level check fails (CR-17)
        VAL-->>UI: Run blocked, failures listed
        UI-->>S: Data Quality Report (RPT-02)
    else All file-level checks pass
        VAL->>DB: Save normalized values beside originals (D2)
        VAL->>AUD: NORMALIZATION events
        RUN->>RUL: Apply exact, bank-originated and carry-in rules
        RUL->>DB: Exact matches, fee and interest items (D4)
        RUL->>AUD: RULE events (rule name, version)
        loop Each unmatched item
            RUN->>SCO: Generate candidates (PRM-02, PRM-04, PRM-05)
            SCO->>SCO: Score features, rank, calibrate confidence
            SCO->>SCO: Build explanation (supporting and conflicting)
            opt GenAI enabled (off by default)
                SCO->>SCO: Add labelled prose via adapter (never scores)
            end
            SCO->>DB: All candidates, scores, confidence (D4)
            SCO->>AUD: AI_RECOMMENDATION event (model version)
        end
        RUN->>RSK: Assess risk (BR-15), classify (EXC), route (BR-13)
        RSK->>DB: Risk, category, queue (D4)
        RSK->>AUD: ROUTING events
        RUN-->>UI: Run ready for review
        UI-->>S: Review queues CAT-01..05
    end
